    "narrative": "With the roster severely thinned by a slate of off-days for core stalwarts like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Bryce Harper**, and **Will Smith**, our remaining active contingent must carry the offensive load today. **Dylan Beavers** stands as our premier start with a 68.38 score, fueled by a favorable pairing against Trey Yesavage. **Dylan Beavers** benefits significantly from hitting at the top of the order and facing a mid-tier arm, with park factors and platoon splits amplifying his baseline projection by nearly 18 points. Similarly, **Jeremiah Jackson** draws the same matchup against Yesavage; while his base projection is slightly more conservative, the +16% park adjustment and his recent consistency make him a high-floor play in the middle of our order.\n\nWe are leaning heavily into platoon advantages and speed dynamics to hunt for stolen bases, our scarcest category. **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.72) is a fascinating play today; while he faces a decent arm in Zebby Matthews, his score is bolstered by a rare confluence of factors: favorable wind, a shift to the #2 hole, and the slow delivery speed of the opposing pitcher, which maximizes his elite sprint-based stolen base potential. **Gleyber Torres** (64.12) rounds out our active starters, capitalizing on a platoon advantage against the left-handed DJ Herz. While we are currently in \"Lineup Pending\" mode for all four, the projected placements are stable. No specific weather flags are present, but with our limited bench depth today, these four must avoid early-game substitutions to protect our games-played cap. If **Lawrence Butler**, **Justin Crawford**, or **Daulton Varsho** had been active, we might have rotated for defensive versatility, but today we rely on the high-efficiency potential of **Gleyber Torres** and company to maintain our roto standing.",
